The function is already near-optimal, so the only gain is making the guard branchless: load the members once and let the compiler emit a conditional move instead of a predictable-but-still-branching early return.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetNum(void) const
{
    const Profile* p = profile;
    return ((p != NULL) && (profileIndex < p->numFields))
               ? p->fields[profileIndex].num
               : static_cast<FIT_UINT8>(FIT_FIELD_NUM_INVALID);
}
```